     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Current guideline:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Surviving Sepsis Campaign international guidelines for sepsis and septic shock, 2026."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sepsis"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is life-threatening organ dysfunction from a dysregulated host response to infection. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Septic shock:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " vasopressors needed to keep MAP ≥ 65 mm Hg and lactate > 2 mmol/L despite adequate fluids."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "qSOFA:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ≥ 2 of respiratory rate ≥ 22, altered mentation, systolic BP ≤ 100 mm Hg calls for further evaluation for sepsis and its source."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Outside the ICU,"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " qSOFA predicts inpatient mortality better than SOFA or SIRS."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Initial tests:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " CBC with differential, comprehensive metabolic panel, lactate, blood cultures, urinalysis and urine culture, and cultures from likely sources."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Fluids:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 1 L crystalloid rapidly; most patients need at least 30 mL/kg in the first 3 hours."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Still hypotensive:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " norepinephrine or vasopressin (up to 0.03 units/minute) may be given to raise mean BP to at least 65 mm Hg."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
 "meta": {
  "title": "Sepsis and septic shock: current definitions and first steps",
  "relevantTo": "Sepsis; Septic shock",
  "written": "2026-10",
  "differs": {
   "doc": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": null
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Your notes (Septic Shock row) define sepsis as SIRS + a focus of infection (lactate > 4), severe sepsis as SIRS + multi-system organ failure, and septic shock as sepsis + refractory hypotension."
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": null
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The current definition is organ dysfunction from a dysregulated response to infection; septic shock means vasopressors for MAP ≥ 65 mm Hg with lactate > 2 mmol/L despite fluids."
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
